#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""caffe: keep the Mac awake, with a coffee bar of your running agent sessions.

Every interactive Copilot CLI / Codex CLI / Claude Code / Pi session gets an
espresso. Each supported desktop application gets a latte named after the app.
Busy agents steam harder. When a session ends, its cup drains and
leaves the counter. A barista cat wanders behind the cups, checks on new and
finished ones, and naps when the bar is quiet.

App lattes show total CPU and RAM. Running local Copilot app sessions and chats
also get individual espressos labeled "Agent"; idle ones are hidden.

The pictures need a terminal with the kitty graphics protocol, such as Ghostty,
kitty, WezTerm or a recent iTerm2. Other terminals get the bar without pictures.
Press q (or Ctrl-C) to close the bar and get your receipt.

`caffe update` installs upstream over this copy, replacing local customizations.
"""

